'The script uses the 'toolbar' function built into Signal, and was created based on the tutorial at https://ced.co.uk/img/SigTrain.pdf (see pages 77-78).
'See also the manual if you need further help on understanding what any given function does (https://ced.co.uk/img/Sig4Scr.pdf).

'This script is designed to provide 'online' measurements of MEP amplitudes
'these measurements are used to set the intensity of the TMS stimulator and modify it until the resting motor threshold is found.
'The current search approach is a binary search algorythm; we reduce the possible intensities by half each time.
'We need to look at minimum of 2 adjacent MSO values (the RMT, aka lowest intensity with at least 5 50uV MEPs, and the RMT-1, aka the highest intensity where we get 6 trials with <50uV MEPs (proving that the RMT is the lowest).
'with a binary search algorythm we should need a maximum of 6 intensities, if we assume:
'   -intensities <20 are not worth examining (too low to reasonably get an MEP, at least in typical adult population)
'   -intensities >90 are not worth examining (the participant is unlikely to be eligible for our study - if we need 110% of RMT, this would be 99% MSO, so we'd likely get overheats etc).
'Note that increasing this range to 1-100% of MSO should only lead to a maximum of 7 intensities being required (binary search cuts down options quickly!).
'in the future we might implement a revised version that takes into account probabilities (most thresholds will be around the mean, presumably with a gaussian distribution)
'this should improve efficiency but have a fairly minor impact (assume min 5 intensities required, max 7).

'TMS intensity is set using the 'SampleState() function alongside the RMT finder configuration supplied.
'States are defined as numbers between 001-199. The first digit refers to the stimulator (0 = main, 1 = auxilary), the remaining 2 refer to the intensity
'   -State 001 would be stimulator 0 (main) at an intensity of 1% of MSO.
'   -State 050 would be stimulator 0 (main) at an intensity of 50%.
'   -State 150 would be stimulator 1 (aux) at an intensity of 50%, and so on.
'in the intial testing phase we are working with one stimulator only, so states can be between 0-99.

'For each intensity we need to take a maximum of 10 trials, and a minimum of 5.
'We don't need 10 trials per intensity because as soon as we have at least 5 trials >=50uV, we know this COULD be the RMT, so we can move to a LOWER intensity.
'By contrast, if we have 6 trials with MEPs <50uV, we know it CANNOT be the RMT, and can move to a HIGHER intensity.
'So the max we would need is 10 trials (some combination of 5 trials <50uV, and 5 trials >=50uV).


'''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''' 
'' USER DEFINED VARIABLES - default values here are provided based on using a magstim Bistim, assuming average RMT = 47% MSO (see data from https://www.brainstimjrnl.com/article/S1935-861X(19)30480-2/fulltext#app-1).
' Number of muscles and ranges for initial search space
var muscles      := 1;                     'how many data channels/muscles are we going to work with? Between 1 and 4 are possible.
var relTestRange := 10;                    'range to search (e.g hotspot intensity +/- 10) if a relative search space is chosen in the dialogue box
var minTestRange := 20;                    'minimum of search range if an absolute search space is chosen in the dialogue box
var maxTestRange := 90;                    'maximum

'Magstim parameters: type of device and corresponding sampling configurations
var magstimType := 1;               'set to 0 for a magstim 200, or 1 for a bistim - note this autoatically sets up the configuration files below

'Trial-level parameters: amplitude to consider valid or invalid, values of noise, windows to calculate baseline noise and MEPs
var requiredAmplitude     := 50;                'peak to peak amplitude in uV that should be met or exceeded to be considered above threshold
var noiseValueLimit       := 10;                'RMS baseline EMG value that should not be exceeded; trial is rejected if above this value
var offsetCorrection      := 1;                 'correct the offset before calculating the noise? 0 = no, 1 = yes; correcting the offset dramatically reduces noise, so it's recommended
var pulseTime             := 0.5;               'by the sampling configuration, the sweep is of length 1 second and the pulse occurs half-way through it (at 0.5 seconds)
var baselineStartTime     := 0.398;             'start time for getting baseline RMS activity
var baselineEndTime       := 0.498;             'end time for getting baseline RMS activity
var MEPstartTime          := 0.510;             'start time at which to begin measuring channel MEP amplitude
var MEPendTime            := 0.550;             'end time to stop measuring channel MEP response
var interTrialTime        := 4.5;               'in seconds, time between trials
var interTrialVariation   := 0;                 'in percentage, variation of the time between trials (e.g. 20% of 5 seconds = 1 second)

'Other parameters
var currentPath$ := FilePath$();   'this sets the path to where the script is
var savePath$ := currentPath$;     'where the log file will be saved to - note this is by default, the folder where this script is
var waitTime := 15;                'seconds to allow the experimenter to place the coil in the correct position before the scri
var debugMode := 0;                'if 1, changes some settings for faster bug checking. If 0 runs normally. Should be 0 for any real testing you do

'''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''' 
'' GLOBAL VARIABLES - these are used at several different times during the script, or represent default values
'The user DOES NOT NEED to make edits to these variables
var data%;                                           'view handle for the data file we will create
var dataChan%[4];                                    'array to hold list of channels we record data from (could increase in theory)
dataChan%[0] := 1;                                   '1st muscle recorded from is on data channel 1
dataChan%[1] := 2;                                   '2nd muscle recorded from is on data channel 2
dataChan%[2] := 3;                                   '3rd muscle recorded from is on data channel 3
dataChan%[3] := 4;                                   '4th muscle recorded from is on data channel 4
var timestampStart, timestampEnd;
var muscleIterator := 0;                             'used to loop through the dataChan array to extract data
var testValue%[4];                                   'holds MEP amplitudes recorded from each data channel the trial
var noiseValue%[4];                                  'holds RMS noise values recorded from each channel for the trial
var noiseFlag := 0;                                  'becomes 1 if the background noise value on the trial was too high
var noisyTrials := 0;                                'keep count of trials with noise
var currentIntensity, minimum, maximum;              'variables to set up the binary search algorithm
var trialNumber := 0;                                'overall trial number (note; this isn't the 'frame' trial number, which we calculate for each intensity
var intensitiesSearched := 1;                        'how many different intensities have we tried?
var trialsAboveRequiredAmplitude := 0;               'how many trials at this intensity were above threshold?
var trialsBelowRequiredAmplitude := 0;               'how many trials at this intensity were below threshold?
var finishedFlag := 0;                               'used to double check all intensities have been tested
var list[10];                                        'array to hold the possible values for RMT (intensities where >=5/10 50uV MEPs found)
var i;
var pauseButtonPressed := 0;                         'boolean for current state of the manual pause button (0 = not pressed, 1 = pressed)
for i := 0 to 9 step 1 do                            'empty array defaults to store 0's - setting this to very high numbers lets us later check for lowest (real) value
    list[i] := 999;
next;


''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''' START OF THE SCRIPT ''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''''


'' INITIALIZATION - used to set up the appearance of the on screen layout & start running the toolbar function
var ok%, nameOfLogFile$, MSO%;
DlgCreate("Enter name of output files");  'start new dialog
DlgString(1, "Enter Particiant ID", 20); 'string, any characters
ok% := DlgShow(nameOfLogFile$);    'show dialog
nameOfLogFile$ := savePath$ + nameOfLogFile$ + ".txt";

DlgCreate ("Hotspot Intensity"); 'start new dialog
DlgInteger(1,"%MSO value of Hotspot (0 = absolute search space)",0, 100, 0, 0, 1);   'range 0-10,spinner
ok% := DlgShow(MSO%); 'show dialog
'PrintLog(MSO%);

if MSO% = 0 then  'default ABSOLUTE & wide search...
    minimum := minTestRange;
    maximum := maxTestRange;
    currentIntensity := round((maximum + minimum)/2);  'set the current state to begin at the starting intensity
else        'target search around hotspot intensity
    currentIntensity := MSO%;
    minimum := MSO% - relTestRange;
    maximum := MSO% + relTestRange;
endif

var startingMinimum := minimum;

EditSelectAll();     'selects any text currently in the log file
EditClear();         'clears text from the log file

'set up width of window for EMG data and log window based on number of muscles
var data_width := 100 - (20 + (muscles * 6)); 'this sets the width of the data, which is reduced as more muscles are tested
var log_width := 100 - data_width;  'conversely, the width of the log file increases to output values for all muscles


'write header line for log text...
var logString$ := "%MSO\tTrial\t";   
for muscleIterator := 0 to muscles-1 do
    logString$ := logString$ + "MEP_" + Str$(muscleIterator+1) + "\t";
next;
for muscleIterator := 0 to muscles-1 do
    logString$ := logString$ + "RMS_" + Str$(muscleIterator+1) + "\t";
next;
logString$ := logString$ + "\r";
PrintLog(logString$);

data%:=FileNew(0,2);           'open a new data file for sampling
WindowVisible(1);              'show the new data file
If data%<0 then                'if you can't start a new file, show an error message
    Message("Unable to open new data file"); 
    Halt; 
endif;   
Window(0,0,data_width,100);   'here we apply the window settings

'set up window settings for log text
FrontView(logHandle());    'select the log text window
Window(data_width, 0, 100, 98); 'here we apply the window settings
FrontView(data%);      'select the log text window, prevents error for recording from the data window

'set up the state parameters (%MSO, inter-trial interval, etc)    
var nStates% := 100;
SampleStates(nStates%);
SampleAuxStateParam(1,magstimType);                   'tells the system there is a magstim device attached, and the type of device
for i := 1 to nStates% do    
    SampleAuxStateValue(i,1,i);                       'for each state, set stimulator A to give the corresponding stimulation intensity (e.g. state 3 = 3% MSO)
    SampleAuxStateValue(i,2,0);                       'for each state, set stimulator B to 0% MSO.
    SampleFixedInt(i, interTrialTime);                'for each state set the intertrial interval in seconds
    SampleFixedVar(i, interTrialVariation);           'for each state set the intertrial variation in percentage
    SampleStateLabel$(i,Print$(i));
    
next;
'SampleState(currentIntensity); 
MakeRMTToolbar();      'creates the toolbar that the user will interact with to make the script work
Halt;

'' SETUP TOOLBAR - modify things here to add buttons and different options in the future (e.g. maybe we can set the starting intensity and minimum/maximum search values here?)
Func MakeRMTToolbar()

    ToolbarClear();                                                                         'clear out any existing toolbars
    ToolbarSet(0,"",doIdle%);                                                               'tells the system what to do when 'idle' between data points being sampled
    ToolbarSet(1, "QUIT RMT-Finder");                                                       'exit button
    ToolbarSet(2, "START RMT-Finder", doStart%);                                            'start button
    return Toolbar("Resting Motor Threshold Finder (RMT-Finder)", 36);                      'name displayed on the toolbar (36 = user may use the view menu + may move and resize the window)
end;



'' START BUTTON PRESSED; start collecting data... - maybe have this auto run..?
Func doStart%()
    Yield(waitTime);                      'wait a few seconds for experimenter to place coil on hotspot
    timestampStart := seconds();          'start timer to measure duration of data collection
    SampleState(currentIntensity);        'set the sample state (i.e. TMS intensity and device) based on the user defined variables
    SampleStart();                        'startSampling
    SampleStatesRun(0);                   'enables manual/direct script control of states
'SampleWrite(0);                          'don't save the file once we finish collecting this frame...
    SamplePause(1);                       'pause sampling - after each frame of data is collected this will trigger the 'idle' function
    return 1;                             'This leaves toolbar active
end;


'' IDLE FUNCTION: used to detect when the stimulator has just finished collecting a frame, also where we determine if we should change intensity
Func doIdle%()

    var s%;
    s% := SampleStatus();
    if (s% = 3) then                                                                        'If paused between sweeps...
    
        if trialNumber = 0 then                                                             'this is the very first trial, which currently is a 'dummy' trial that's not of use for our analysis
            SampleState(currentIntensity);                                                  'set the stimulator to the correct intensity it should use for the first real trial
            trialNumber := trialNumber + 1;                                                 'increment the trial number so we know to continue
            SampleSweep();                                                                  'trigger next frame (after delay based on configuration file)
        else
            trialNumber := trialNumber + 1;                                                 'we just recorded a frame/trial, so increment the (total) trial number.
        
        'get data from data channels for each muscle being recorded from:  'MARCOS: below you multiply the signal by *1000 to put it in microV, this assumes Signal is configured in mV... should we say it at the beginning?
        for muscleIterator := 0 to muscles-1 do                                                                                         'loop through muscles being recorded from
            testValue%[muscleIterator] := Round(ChanMeasure(dataChan%[muscleIterator] , 9, MEPstartTime, MEPendTime) * 1000);              'read MEP peak to peak amplitude
            noiseValue%[muscleIterator]:= Round(ChanMeasure(dataChan%[muscleIterator],10,baselineStartTime,baselineEndTime) * 1000);   'read RMS noise from muscle in baseline time period
            ' correct offset before calculating noise
            if offsetCorrection = 1 then         
                var baselineMean := ChanMeasure(dataChan%[muscleIterator], 2, baselineStartTime, baselineEndTime);
                ChanOffset(dataChan%[muscleIterator], -baselineMean);
                noiseValue%[muscleIterator] := Round(ChanMeasure(dataChan%[muscleIterator], 10, baselineStartTime, baselineEndTime) * 1000);
            endif
        next;
        
        'check background noise is below threshold for each channel
        noiseFlag := 0;
        for muscleIterator := 0 to muscles-1 do
            if noiseValue%[muscleIterator] > noiseValueLimit then
                noiseFlag := 1;
                noisyTrials := noisyTrials + 1;
            endif
        next;
        
       'check if all muscles being recorded from are above required amplitude value & modify counts accordingly (if noise threshold exceeded then don't increment these counts).                           
        var musclesPassed := 0;
        if noiseFlag = 0 then
            for muscleIterator := 0 to muscles-1 do
                if testValue%[muscleIterator] >= requiredAmplitude then
                    musclesPassed := musclesPassed + 1;
                endif
            next;
            if musclesPassed = muscles then                                                 'each muscle checked was >= required threshold, so the trial is 'valid'
                trialsAboveRequiredAmplitude := trialsAboveRequiredAmplitude + 1;
            else
                trialsBelowRequiredAmplitude := trialsBelowRequiredAmplitude + 1;
            endif
        else
            printLog("Noise too high; the trial below is NOT counted\n");
        endif
        
        'build string to write readouts to log text: 
        
        logString$ := Str$(currentIntensity);                                               'start with current intensity being checked      
        logString$ := logString$ + "\t" + Str$(trialsAboveRequiredAmplitude + trialsBelowRequiredAmplitude) + "\t"; 'add trial number (based on trials with acceptable noise levels only)
        
        for muscleIterator := 0 to muscles-1 do   
            logString$ := logString$ + Str$(testValue%[muscleIterator]) + "\t";             'add readouts of MEP amplitudes from each channel in adjacent columnns
        next;
  
        for muscleIterator := 0 to muscles-1 do                                               
            logString$ := logString$ + Str$(noiseValue%[muscleIterator]) + "\t";            'add noise value readouts in adjacent columns:
        next;
        logString$ := logString$ + "\r";                                                    'move to new line
        
        PrintLog(logString$);                                                               'output text to log file    
        
        if trialsAboveRequiredAmplitude = 5 or trialsBelowRequiredAmplitude = 6 then
    
            if trialsAboveRequiredAmplitude = 5 then                                        '5 MEPs above 50uV, so possible RMT found
                list[intensitiesSearched] := currentIntensity;                              'Add this to list of possible RMT values
                maximum := currentIntensity - 1;                                            'only test intensities lower than this from now on
                if maximum < minimum then
                    maximum := minimum;                                                      'only occurs if the last intensity checked was the minimum; should end testing when checking for finishedFlag variable
                endif
            endif
        
            if trialsBelowRequiredAmplitude = 6 then                                        '6 MEPs below 50uV, this can't be the RMT - shift TMS intensity UP
                minimum := currentIntensity + 1;                                            'only intensities higher than this should be tested from now on
                if minimum > maximum then
                    minimum := maximum;
                endif
                
            endif
            
            if currentIntensity = maximum and maximum = minimum then
                finishedFlag := 1;
            endif
            
            currentIntensity := round((maximum + minimum)/2);                               'apply algorithm to determine next intensity to work at
            SampleState(currentIntensity);                                                  'set stimulator to try next intensity
            intensitiesSearched := intensitiesSearched + 1;                                 'we are going to search a new intensity, so increment this number
            trialsAboveRequiredAmplitude := 0;                                              'resetting values
            trialsBelowRequiredAmplitude := 0;                                              'resetting values
            PrintLog("\n");                                                                 'add a new line to separate out trials with different intensities
            'PrintLog("Minimum = ", minimum, " Maximum = ", maximum);                        'check values...
        endif

            'check for intensities left to examine
            'if maximum - minimum > 0 or currentIntensity = list[Min(list)]-1 then           'we haven't yet exhausted all possible options, so keep testing...        BUT This is where we check if max > min, so we need to trigger the 'getout' here
            if finishedFlag = 0 then
                SampleSweep();      'tell signal it can proceed to the next sweep (it'll wait until the time defined in the config file before starting)
            else                                                                            'all possible intensities searched; provide final output for user.
                TimestampEnd := seconds();                                                  'end timer for data collection
                trialNumber := trialNumber - 1;
                intensitiesSearched := intensitiesSearched - 1;
                printLog("Search complete!\n");
                printLog("RMT = ", list[Min(list)]); 
                PrintLog("Intensities examined = ", intensitiesSearched);
                PrintLog("Total trials = ", trialNumber);
                PrintLog("Noisy trials = ", noisyTrials);        
                PrintLog("Time taken (seconds)= ", round(TimestampEnd - TimestampStart));   'calculate & output duration from first to last trial in seconds  
                FrontView(logHandle());                                                     'select the log text window       
                Speak("Data collection complete");   
                
                if list[Min(list)] = 999 then
                    Speak("Warning, range too low");  'MARCOS: modified this message and the equivalent below to be shorter
                PrintLog("WARNING! RMT was not detected. Increase the starting intensity and/or increase range and try again.");     
                endif
            
                if list[Min(list)] = startingMinimum then
                    Speak("Warning, range too high");  
                    PrintLog("WARNING! RMT was not detected. Decrease the starting intensity and/or increase the range and try again.");
                endif                 
                             
                FileSaveAs(nameOfLogFile$); 
                Halt;
            
            endif 'of check for intensities left to examine
        endif 'check of trial number
    endif   'of paused between sweeps  'might be an error here..?
    return 1  'This leaves toolbar active

end